   "evidence": "The theorem proves only `e6MinusculeWeight 0 \u2218 graphPermE6 \u2209 range e6MinusculeWeight`; the construction it feeds requires `hwt : \u2200 i k, wt (basisPerm i) (torusPerm k) = wt i k` plus `hbasis : \u2200 i, \u03b8 (b i) = b (basisPerm i)` (TauCeti/Algebra/Lie/UniversalEnveloping/Kostant/RootSubgroup/Scheme/ToralClosure/NumberedSymmetry.lean:110-112), i.e. sufficiency for a basis-permutation realization, not necessity of any automorphism of the carrier.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/RootSystem/SimplyConnectedRootDatum/E6/MinusculeWeight.lean",
   "fix": "Restate as: \"So the numbered-symmetry construction does not apply to this weight family: the automorphism is not realized by a permutation of the weight basis of V(\u03d6\u2081).\"",
   "issue": "Docstring of `e6MinusculeWeight_zero_comp_graphPermE6_notMem_range` concludes \"So a carrier built from this weight family alone does not inherit the diagram automorphism.\" That is false: the graph automorphism is an automorphism of the simply connected E\u2086 group scheme however it is realized; what the theorem shows is only that the equivariance hypothesis `hwt` of the numbered-symmetry construction fails, so the automorphism is not realized by the coordinate permutation on this weight basis.",
